ect":true,"choice":"Decreasing tail wind increases lift and a/c rises above the glide path"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc85","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Weakening head wind raises aircraft above the flight path"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f002a4","question":"During which months does Tamil Nadu receive most of its rainfall?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc86","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Oct - Nov"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc87","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Jul - Sep"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc88","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Apr - Jun"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc89","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Dec - Mar"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f002ac","question":"If there is a hole in the radar echo along a line of thunderstorms, what does it indicate?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc8a","isCorrect":false,"choice":"No precipitation"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc8b","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Strong convective activity"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc8c","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Area free of clouds"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc8d","isCorrect":false,"choice":"A gap between two CB"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f00281","question":"CAT is most pronounced on which side of the subtropical jet stream?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc8e","isCorrect":false,"choice":"About 3 km above the core"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc8f","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Cold side of core"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc90","isCorrect":false,"choice":"South side of core"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc91","isCorrect":false,"choice":"at core"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f002a8","question":"How is station-level pressure at an ARP reduced to mean sea level?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc92","isCorrect":false,"choice":"ISA is QFF"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc93","isCorrect":false,"choice":"ISA is QFE"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc94","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Isothermal is QNH"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc95","isCorrect":true,"choice":"ISA is QNH"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f00282","question":"How does hail form from supercooled water droplets?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc96","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Condensation"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc97","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Deposition"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc98","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Evaporation"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc99","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Transpiration"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f002a2","question":"During southwest monsoon, how do winds behave above 500 hPa?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc9a","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Ely over S weak Wly over N India"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc9b","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Wly over S and strong over N India"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc9c","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Wly over S and weak Wly over N India"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc9d","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Strong Ely over S weak over N India"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f002a5","question":"How does the ITCZ affect India’s weather?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc9e","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Winters only"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abc9f","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Pre - monsoon only"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abca0","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Monsoon only"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abca1","isCorrect":true,"choice":"All the four seasons"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f0027e","question":"Why is gradient wind weaker than geostrophic wind around a low?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abca2","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Centripetal force is provided by pressure gradient force"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abca3","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Centripetal force is added to the pressure gradient force"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abca4","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Coriolis force is added to the pressure gradient force"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abca5","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Coriolis force is opposite to centripetal"}],"explanation":"<h3 class=\"\" data-start=\"737\" data-end=\"766\">💨 Force Balance in a Low</h3>\\n<ul data-start=\"768\" data-end=\"961\">\\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"768\" data-end=\"870\">\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"770\" data-end=\"870\"><strong data-start=\"770\" data-end=\"781\">P (PGF)</strong> and <strong data-start=\"786\" data-end=\"811\">C (centripetal force)</strong> are both directed <strong data-start=\"830\" data-end=\"840\">inward</strong> toward the center of the low.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"871\" data-end=\"958\">\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"873\" data-end=\"958\">The <strong data-start=\"877\" data-end=\"899\">Coriolis force (f)</strong> acts <strong data-start=\"905\" data-end=\"916\">outward</strong>, trying to push air away from the center.</p>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"962\" data-end=\"993\">So to maintain circular motion:</p>\\n<ul data-start=\"994\" data-end=\"1081\">\\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"994\" data-end=\"1078\">\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"996\" data-end=\"1078\">The <strong data-start=\"1000\" data-end=\"1017\">inward forces</strong> (P + C) must <strong data-start=\"1031\" data-end=\"1042\">balance</strong> the <strong data-start=\"1047\" data-end=\"1077\">outward Coriolis force (f)</strong>.</p>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1082\" data-end=\"1267\">But wait — <strong data-start=\"1093\" data-end=\"1141\">centripetal force isn’t an independent force</strong>; it comes from the curved path of the air and is provided by part of the pressure gradient.</p>\\n<hr class=\"\" data-start=\"1269\" data-end=\"1272\">\\n<h3 class=\"\" data-start=\"1274\" data-end=\"1290\">🧠 Key Idea:</h3>\\n<ul data-start=\"1292\" data-end=\"1564\">\\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"1292\" data-end=\"1445\">\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1294\" data-end=\"1445\">Part of the pressure gradient (P) goes into creating the necessary curvature (C), and only the <strong data-start=\"1389\" data-end=\"1412\">remaining part of P</strong> balances the Coriolis force (f).</p>\\n</li>\\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"1446\" data-end=\"1564\">\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1448\" data-end=\"1564\">So, effectively, <strong data-start=\"1465\" data-end=\"1474\">P &lt; f</strong> when you look at how much of the pressure gradient is left to balance the Coriolis force.</p>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1566\" data-end=\"1577\">Now, since:</p>\\n<ul data-start=\"1578\" data-end=\"1648\">\\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"1578\" data-end=\"1624\">\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1580\" data-end=\"1624\">Coriolis force <strong data-start=\"1595\" data-end=\"1624\">increases with wind speed</strong></p>\\n</li>\\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"1625\" data-end=\"1648\">\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1627\" data-end=\"1648\">And we have <strong data-start=\"1639\" data-end=\"1648\">P &lt; f</strong></p>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1650\" data-end=\"1803\">This means the wind speed (V) must be <strong data-start=\"1688\" data-end=\"1696\">less</strong> than what it would be if only P and f were balancing each other — that is, the <strong data-start=\"1776\" data-end=\"1796\">geostrophic wind</strong> speed.</p>\\n<hr class=\"\" data-start=\"1805\" data-end=\"1808\">\\n<blockquote data-start=\"1835\" data-end=\"2175\">\\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"2085\" data-end=\"2175\"></p></blockquote>\\n","subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f00280","question":"What is the typical validity period for TAF and TREND?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abca6","isCorrect":true,"choice":"9 hr; 2 hr"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abca7","isCorrect":false,"choice":"24 hr; 3 hr"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abca8","isCorrect":false,"choice":"12 hr; 2 hr"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abca9","isCorrect":false,"choice":"24 hr; 9 hr"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f00283","question":"How does thermal wind blow relative to isobars, and which way is left?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcaa","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Isotherms, low temperature"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcab","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Isobars, low temperature"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcac","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Isobars, low pressure"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcad","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Isallobars, high temperature"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f002ab","question":"What is the difference between an airmass thunderstorm (AM TS) and a steady-state thunderstorm (SS TS)?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcae","isCorrect":true,"choice":"SS TS duration is more"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcaf","isCorrect":false,"choice":"AM TS duration is more"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcb0","isCorrect":false,"choice":"SS TS duration is less"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcb1","isCorrect":false,"choice":"AM TS occur in fronts"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f00295","question":"Why is a calm, clear night cooler than a cloudy night?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcb2","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Clouds prevent terrestrial radiations from escaping"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcb3","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Clouds radiate heat towards sky"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcb4","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Due to CO2 and H2O present in the air"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcb5","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Terrestrial radiation skip through clouds"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f00299","question":"Why do no cyclonic or high-pressure systems form within 5° of the equator?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcb6","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Pressure gradient force is negligible"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcb7","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Frictional force is minimal"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcb8","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Coriolis force is negligible"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcb9","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Geotropic force is maximum"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f0027f","question":"If an aircraft altimeter is set to QFE before landing, what will it read on touchdown?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcba","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Height of A/C wheels above runway"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcbb","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Flight level"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcbc","isCorrect":false,"choice":"A/C altitude AMSL"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcbd","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Height of A/C above ARP in ISA"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f0028d","question":"Give an example of non-frontal atmospheric stability.","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcbe","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Squall line"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcbf","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Inversion"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcc0","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Frontogenesis"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcc1","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Occlusion"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f00292","question":"How is wind 260102 KT reported in METAR/SPECI?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcc2","isCorrect":false,"choice":"260102 KT + 26002 KT"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcc3","isCorrect":false,"choice":"260P99 KT only"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcc4","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Only in remark column"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcc5","isCorrect":true,"choice":"260P99 KT and complete wind in remark column"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","explanation":"","_id":"682e9d56d715cc08c3f00297","question":"How is density altitude defined?","choices":[{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcc6","isCorrect":true,"choice":"Higher if atmosphere is warmer than ISA"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcc7","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Lower if atmosphere is warmer than ISA"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcc8","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Higher if atmosphere is colder than ISA"},{"_id":"693e81576a1995dddc7abcc9","isCorrect":false,"choice":"Higher if atmosphere is isothermal"}],"subject":"Meteorology","book":"Pilot Shala Practice Set","topic":"Miscellaneous"}]